{%- comment -%}
  Hartwick Atelier — 01 PRODUCT (three columns).
  Built to `04_HA_Product_Desktop_REVISED_EDITABLE.pdf`, Aloha's revised
  wireframe, on a 1440 x 6102 canvas measured at 1:1. Geometry below is that
  drawing, not an estimate:

      left rail   58 -> 380   (322)   sticky
      gap                      42
      media rail  422 -> 1066 (644)   scrolls
      gap                      57
      buy rail   1123 -> 1390 (267)   sticky

  WHY THIS IS A CUSTOM SECTION, when the rest of the build is native.
  Luxe's `main-product` renders `.product-main-top-section` as a flex box with
  exactly TWO children — a media section and an info section. The revised design
  needs THREE columns with two independently sticky rails on either side of a
  scrolling one. No arrangement of CSS gets a flex item's children to straddle a
  sibling, and `display: contents` on the info section would break the very
  stickiness the design is built around. So this is the case CLAUDE.md reserves
  for custom work: "custom sections only where they don't [meet the requirement]".

  WHAT IS STILL SHOPIFY'S OWN. The parts that carry money and inventory are not
  reimplemented — they are Luxe's own snippets, called with the same arguments
  `main-product` uses:

      snippets/product-variant-picker.liquid   variants, availability, swatches
      snippets/buy-buttons.liquid              the product form, cart JS, errors

  Between them they read four settings from their calling section
  (`gallery_aspect_ratio`, `color_scheme`, and two sticky-button flags) and two
  from `block` (`picker_type`, `show_puncuation`, `show_dynamic_checkout`,
  `show_gift_card_recipient`). All six are declared in the schema below and
  `block: section` passes them through, so the snippets behave exactly as they
  do on the native template. Variants, inventory, analytics and checkout are
  untouched.

  TERMINOLOGY (CLAUDE.md). The heading is the permanent numbered Style; the line
  beneath it is the material; the Expression is a labelled row in the buy rail.
  The Lot is customer-facing as a Roman numeral. No Edition number renders
  unless the garment is individually numbered — see snippets/ha-pdp-identity.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign product_form_id = 'product-form-' | append: section.id
  assign mf = product.metafields.hartwick

  assign style_name = product.title
  if mf.style.value.display_name != blank
    assign style_name = mf.style.value.display_name
  endif

  # The line under the Style name is the cloth, not the colourway: the design
  # prints "HANDSPUN SILK & LINEN" there and puts "Natural / Undyed" — the
  # Expression — in the buy rail as a labelled row.
  assign cloth = mf.fibre | default: section.settings.ph_cloth

  # The Lot, customer-facing as a Roman numeral (Framework v3). With the Edition
  # gone, this is the opening label Aloha asked for: "If the garments are not
  # individually numbered, the opening label should simply show the confirmed Lot
  # information." It renders only when a real Lot exists — never a placeholder.
  assign lot_label = ''
  if mf.lot.value.number_roman != blank
    assign lot_label = 'Lot ' | append: mf.lot.value.number_roman
  endif

  # Key facts. Each renders only when present; an absent field leaves no
  # orphaned label and no gap.
  assign fact_fibre = mf.fibre | default: section.settings.ph_fibre
  assign fact_weave = mf.weave | default: section.settings.ph_weave
  assign fact_colour = mf.colour_name | default: section.settings.ph_colour
  assign fact_made = ''
  if mf.place_of_construction.value.place != blank
    assign fact_made = mf.place_of_construction.value.place
  else
    assign fact_made = section.settings.ph_made_in
  endif

  assign expression = mf.expression | default: section.settings.ph_expression

  # Availability is a fact, never a countdown. Aloha, 3 Sep 2026: "We do not
  # want to turn that reality into scarcity language."
  assign availability = mf.availability_note | default: section.settings.ph_availability
  assign ship_date = mf.expected_ship_date | default: section.settings.ph_ship_date

  assign fit_a = mf.fit | default: section.settings.ph_fit_line_one
  assign fit_b = ''
  if mf.model_height != blank and mf.size_worn != blank
    assign fit_b = 'Model is ' | append: mf.model_height | append: ' and wears ' | append: mf.size_worn | append: '.'
  else
    assign fit_b = section.settings.ph_fit_line_two
  endif

  assign is_placeholder = false
  if mf.style.value.display_name == blank or mf.fibre == blank or mf.expression == blank
    assign is_placeholder = true
  endif

  # The rail shows an excerpt; the full description becomes an accordion row when
  # it is longer than the excerpt, so nothing is lost and nothing is buried.
  assign full_description = product.description
  if full_description == blank
    assign full_description = section.settings.ph_intro
  endif
  assign plain_description = full_description | strip_html | strip
  assign intro_excerpt = plain_description | truncatewords: section.settings.intro_words
  assign description_is_long = false
  if plain_description.size > intro_excerpt.size
    assign description_is_long = true
  endif
-%}

{%- comment -%}
  Luxe's product form is a set of custom elements — <product-info>, <variant-selects>,
  <product-form> — driven by product-info.js and product-form.js, and styled by
  section-main-product.css / component-price.css. main-product.liquid loads all of
  these itself. This section reuses the same snippets, so it loads the same assets
  and wraps the rail in the same <product-info> the snippets expect as an ancestor
  (variant changes, availability, price and the cart all resolve through it).
{%- endcomment -%}
<script src="{{ 'product-info.js' | asset_url }}" defer="defer"></script>
<script src="{{ 'product-form.js' | asset_url }}" defer="defer"></script>
{{ 'section-main-product.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
{{ 'component-accordion.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
{{ 'component-price.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
{{ 'component-loading-overlay.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

<product-info
  id="MainProduct-{{ section.id }}"
  class="ha-section ha-pdp"
  data-section="{{ section.id }}"
  data-product-id="{{ product.id }}"
  data-update-url="true"
  data-url="{{ product.url }}"
  data-section-id="{{ section.id }}"
>
  <div class="ha-pdp__grid">

    {%- comment -%} ---------- LEFT RAIL (sticky) ---------- {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="ha-pdp__rail ha-pdp__rail--left">
      <div class="ha-pdp__rail-inner">

        {%- if section.settings.show_breadcrumb -%}
          <nav class="ha-pdp__crumbs ha-record" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
            <a href="{{ routes.collections_url }}">{{ section.settings.crumb_root }}</a>
            {%- if collection.title != blank -%}
              <span aria-hidden="true"> / </span>
              <a href="{{ collection.url }}">{{ collection.title }}</a>
            {%- elsif section.settings.crumb_leaf != blank -%}
              <span aria-hidden="true"> / </span>{{ section.settings.crumb_leaf }}
            {%- endif -%}
            {%- if lot_label != blank -%}
              <span aria-hidden="true"> / </span><span class="ha-pdp__lot">{{ lot_label }}</span>
            {%- endif -%}
          </nav>
        {%- elsif lot_label != blank -%}
          <p class="ha-pdp__crumbs ha-record"><span class="ha-pdp__lot">{{ lot_label }}</span></p>
        {%- endif -%}

        <h1 class="ha-pdp__title ha-identify">{{ style_name }}</h1>

        {%- if cloth != blank -%}
          <p class="ha-pdp__cloth ha-record">{{ cloth }}</p>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- comment -%}
          A SHORT opening only. Aloha: when the purchase information runs long the
          visitor can only finish reading it after scrolling past every image, so
          the long copy moves into the accordion rows below. The excerpt is the
          first sentences; the whole description is the "Description" row.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- if intro_excerpt != blank -%}
          <div class="ha-pdp__intro ha-body ha-narrate">{{ intro_excerpt }}</div>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- if fact_fibre != blank or fact_weave != blank or fact_colour != blank or fact_made != blank -%}
          <dl class="ha-pdp__facts ha-record">
            {%- if fact_fibre != blank -%}<div><dt>Fibre</dt><dd>{{ fact_fibre }}</dd></div>{%- endif -%}
            {%- if fact_weave != blank -%}<div><dt>Weave</dt><dd>{{ fact_weave }}</dd></div>{%- endif -%}
            {%- if fact_colour != blank -%}<div><dt>Colour</dt><dd>{{ fact_colour }}</dd></div>{%- endif -%}
            {%- if fact_made != blank -%}<div><dt>Made in</dt><dd>{{ fact_made }}</dd></div>{%- endif -%}
          </dl>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- if section.settings.record_anchor != blank -%}
          <a class="ha-pdp__record-link ha-record" href="{{ section.settings.record_anchor }}">
            {{ section.settings.record_link_text }}
            <span class="ha-pdp__arrow" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          </a>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- if fit_a != blank or fit_b != blank -%}
          <div class="ha-pdp__fit">
            <h2 class="ha-pdp__fit-title ha-narrate">{{ section.settings.fit_heading }}</h2>
            {%- if fit_a != blank -%}<p class="ha-record">{{ fit_a }}</p>{%- endif -%}
            {%- if fit_b != blank -%}<p class="ha-record">{{ fit_b }}</p>{%- endif -%}
          </div>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- comment -%}
          Two quiet rows close the left rail. Luxe's own accordion markup and its
          global.js behaviour — see snippets/ha-panel-row.liquid for why this is
          the theme's accordion rather than a second one.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- if description_is_long -%}
          {%- capture description_body -%}
            <div class="ha-pdp__row-body ha-body ha-narrate">{{ full_description }}</div>
          {%- endcapture -%}
          {%- render 'ha-panel-row', id: 'description', title: section.settings.description_row_title, content: description_body -%}
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
          {%- if block.type == 'left_row' -%}
            {%- capture row_body -%}
              {%- if block.settings.content != blank -%}
                <div class="ha-pdp__row-body ha-body ha-narrate">{{ block.settings.content }}</div>
              {%- endif -%}
              {%- if block.settings.page != blank -%}
                <div class="ha-pdp__row-body ha-body ha-narrate">{{ block.settings.page.content }}</div>
              {%- endif -%}
            {%- endcapture -%}
            {%- render 'ha-panel-row', id: block.id, title: block.settings.heading, content: row_body -%}
          {%- endif -%}
        {%- endfor -%}

        {%- if is_placeholder -%}
          {%- render 'ha-placeholder-note', show: section.settings.show_placeholder_note,
            text: 'Placeholder — Style, cloth and Expression publish from hartwick.* metafields' -%}
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
    </div>

    {%- comment -%} ---------- MEDIA RAIL (scrolls) ---------- {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="ha-pdp__media">
      {%- if product.media.size > 0 -%}
        <ha-media-rail class="ha-pdp__rail-media" data-count="{{ product.media.size }}">
          <div class="ha-pdp__frames">
            {%- for media in product.media -%}
              <figure class="ha-pdp__frame" id="{{ section.id }}-frame-{{ forloop.index }}">
                {%- if media.media_type == 'image' -%}
                  {%- assign frame_loading = 'lazy' -%}
                  {%- if forloop.first -%}{%- assign frame_loading = 'eager' -%}{%- endif -%}
                  {%- assign frame_alt = media.alt | default: style_name -%}
                  {{ media
                    | image_url: width: 1400
                    | image_tag:
                      loading: frame_loading,
                      sizes: '(min-width: 990px) 45vw, 100vw',
                      widths: '480, 720, 960, 1200, 1400',
                      alt: frame_alt,
                      class: 'ha-pdp__img' }}
                {%- else -%}
                  {{ media | media_tag: image_size: '1400x' }}
                {%- endif -%}
              </figure>
            {%- endfor -%}
          </div>

          {%- comment -%}
            Position markers, one per frame. The design draws them over the
            image's right edge. They are real buttons, not decoration: the rail
            is a scroller and this is the only way to jump within it without a
            mouse wheel.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- if product.media.size > 1 -%}
            <ol class="ha-pdp__dots" aria-label="Product images">
              {%- for media in product.media -%}
                <li>
                  <button
                    type="button"
                    class="ha-pdp__dot"
                    data-frame="{{ section.id }}-frame-{{ forloop.index }}"
                    aria-current="{% if forloop.first %}true{% else %}false{% endif %}"
                  ><span class="visually-hidden">{{ 'products.product.media.load_image' | t: index: forloop.index }}</span></button>
                </li>
              {%- endfor -%}
            </ol>
          {%- endif -%}
        </ha-media-rail>
      {%- else -%}
        {%- render 'ha-figure', label: section.settings.ph_media_label, class: 'ha-pdp__frame ha-pdp__frame--empty' -%}
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>

    {%- comment -%} ---------- BUY RAIL (sticky) ---------- {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="ha-pdp__rail ha-pdp__rail--buy{% if section.settings.enable_sticky_buttons %} sticky-buy-buttons sticky-buy-buttons--border-{{ section.settings.sticky_buttons_border }}{% endif %}">
      <div class="ha-pdp__rail-inner">

        <div class="ha-pdp__price">
          {%- render 'price', product: product, use_variant: true, show_badges: false, price_class: '' -%}
        </div>
        {%- if section.settings.tax_note != blank -%}
          <p class="ha-pdp__tax ha-record">{{ section.settings.tax_note }}</p>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- if expression != blank -%}
          <div class="ha-pdp__field">
            <p class="ha-pdp__field-label ha-record">Expression</p>
            <p class="ha-pdp__field-value ha-pdp__field-value--lead ha-narrate">{{ expression }}</p>
          </div>
        {%- endif -%}

        <div class="ha-pdp__size">
          {%- if section.settings.size_guide_page != blank -%}
            <a class="ha-pdp__size-guide ha-record" href="{{ section.settings.size_guide_page.url }}">Size guide</a>
          {%- endif -%}
          {%- render 'product-variant-picker',
            product: product,
            block: section,
            product_form_id: product_form_id,
            labels: true,
            pill_threshold: 12,
            pill_options_display: 'all',
            show_variant_images: false,
            swatches: false -%}
        </div>

        {%- if availability != blank -%}
          <div class="ha-pdp__field">
            <p class="ha-pdp__field-label ha-record">Availability</p>
            <p class="ha-pdp__field-value ha-pdp__field-value--lead ha-record">{{ availability }}</p>
          </div>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- if ship_date != blank -%}
          <div class="ha-pdp__field">
            <p class="ha-pdp__field-label ha-record">Expected to ship</p>
            <p class="ha-pdp__field-value ha-record">{{ ship_date }}</p>
          </div>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- render 'buy-buttons',
          block: section,
          product: product,
          product_form_id: product_form_id,
          section_id: section.id,
          style: 'solid',
          show_payment_methods: false,
          show_pickup_availability: false -%}

        {%- render 'ha-appointment', text: section.settings.appointment_text -%}

        {%- comment -%}
          The longer purchase terms are a row, not a paragraph, so the buy rail
          stays short enough to read without scrolling the media.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
          {%- if block.type == 'buy_row' -%}
            {%- capture buy_body -%}
              {%- if block.settings.content != blank -%}
                <div class="ha-pdp__row-body ha-body ha-narrate">{{ block.settings.content }}</div>
              {%- endif -%}
              {%- if block.settings.page != blank -%}
                <div class="ha-pdp__row-body ha-body ha-narrate">{{ block.settings.page.content }}</div>
              {%- endif -%}
            {%- endcapture -%}
            {%- render 'ha-panel-row', id: block.id, title: block.settings.heading, content: buy_body -%}
          {%- endif -%}
        {%- endfor -%}

        {%- if section.settings.payment_note != blank -%}
          <p class="ha-pdp__payment ha-record">{{ section.settings.payment_note }}</p>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</product-info>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "HA — Product",
  "tag": "section",
  "class": "ha-section-wrapper",
  "settings": [
    { "type": "paragraph", "content": "Three columns: a sticky left rail, a scrolling media rail and a sticky buy rail. Built to Wireframe 04 (revised)." },

    { "type": "header", "content": "Breadcrumb" },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "show_breadcrumb", "label": "Show breadcrumb", "default": true },
    { "type": "text", "id": "crumb_root", "label": "Root label", "default": "Collection" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "crumb_leaf", "label": "Fallback leaf", "default": "Apparel", "info": "Used when the visitor did not arrive from a collection." },

    { "type": "header", "content": "Left rail" },
    { "type": "richtext", "id": "ph_intro", "label": "Description fallback", "info": "Used only when the product has no description.", "default": "<p><em>Placeholder — the product description publishes from Shopify.</em></p>" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "fit_heading", "label": "Fit heading", "default": "Fit" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "record_link_text", "label": "Record link text", "default": "View the material record" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "record_anchor", "label": "Record link target", "default": "#the-material-record" },
    { "type": "range", "id": "intro_words", "label": "Description excerpt length", "min": 12, "max": 80, "step": 2, "unit": "wd", "default": 32, "info": "The rail shows this many words; the full description opens in a row beneath." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "description_row_title", "label": "Description row title", "default": "Description" },

    { "type": "header", "content": "Buy rail" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "tax_note", "label": "Tax note", "default": "Duties and taxes shown at checkout" },
    { "type": "page", "id": "size_guide_page", "label": "Size guide page" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "appointment_text", "label": "Appointment link", "default": "Request Private Appointment" },
    { "type": "textarea", "id": "payment_note", "label": "Payment note", "default": "Full payment is taken when the order is placed. Delivery timing is shown before checkout." },

    { "type": "header", "content": "Media" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "ph_media_label", "label": "Placeholder label", "default": "Product image / centre media rail" },

    { "type": "header", "content": "Placeholder content", "info": "Used per field, only where the product has no value. Wireframe copy — provenance is unverified and must not go live as fact (risk R7)." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "ph_cloth", "label": "Cloth line", "default": "Handspun silk & linen" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "ph_fibre", "label": "Fibre", "default": "Silk / linen" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "ph_weave", "label": "Weave", "default": "Handwoven" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "ph_colour", "label": "Colour", "default": "Natural / undyed" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "ph_made_in", "label": "Made in", "default": "India" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "ph_expression", "label": "Expression", "default": "Natural / Undyed" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "ph_availability", "label": "Availability", "default": "Made in small quantities" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "ph_ship_date", "label": "Expected to ship" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "ph_fit_line_one", "label": "Fit line 1", "default": "Relaxed through the body." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "ph_fit_line_two", "label": "Fit line 2" },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "show_placeholder_note", "label": "Show placeholder notice", "default": true },

    { "type": "header", "content": "Shopify form (read by Luxe's own snippets)", "info": "These are the settings snippets/product-variant-picker.liquid and snippets/buy-buttons.liquid read from their calling section. Leave them alone unless the form misbehaves." },
    { "type": "select", "id": "picker_type", "label": "Size picker", "options": [{ "value": "button", "label": "Buttons" }, { "value": "dropdown", "label": "Dropdown" }], "default": "button" },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "show_puncuation", "label": "Punctuation after labels", "default": false },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "show_dynamic_checkout", "label": "Dynamic checkout buttons", "default": false },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "show_gift_card_recipient", "label": "Gift card recipient form", "default": false },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "enable_sticky_buttons", "label": "Sticky Add to Bag (mobile)", "default": true, "info": "Required by the mobile brief. Pins the buy form to the bottom of the viewport below 990px." },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "sticky_buttons_border", "label": "Hairline above the sticky bar", "default": true },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "enable_sticky_buttons_desktop", "label": "Sticky Add to Bag (desktop)", "default": false },
    { "type": "select", "id": "gallery_aspect_ratio", "label": "Variant image ratio", "options": [{ "value": "portrait-4x6", "label": "Portrait 2:3" }, { "value": "portrait", "label": "Portrait 4:5" }, { "value": "square", "label": "Square" }], "default": "portrait-4x6" }
  ],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "buy_row",
      "name": "Buy rail row",
      "settings": [
        { "type": "text", "id": "heading", "label": "Heading", "default": "Delivery" },
        { "type": "richtext", "id": "content", "label": "Content" },
        { "type": "page", "id": "page", "label": "Or take the content from a page" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "left_row",
      "name": "Left rail row",
      "settings": [
        { "type": "text", "id": "heading", "label": "Heading", "default": "Sizing information" },
        { "type": "richtext", "id": "content", "label": "Content" },
        { "type": "page", "id": "page", "label": "Or take the content from a page" }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "presets": [{ "name": "Hartwick — Product" }]
}
{% endschema %}
